    "scope": "July 2013 exterior of the former ESMA Officers’ Quarters, the building that later became the ESMA Museum and Site of Memory. Includes the avenue entrance, white plaster and exposed brick, clay roofs, three connected arms and the two open rear courts. The wider former naval campus and the 2015 exhibit structures are outside the 2013 scope.",
    "notes": "The two exact July 2013 originals document plaster and dark window shutters, a low tall-window arm and higher terracotta roofs. Argentina’s nomination documents the pitched roofs, exposed brick central corners and rectangular brick-pier porch. Approximate portions include the main entrance proportions, elevations and exact wing-height assignment."
  },
